WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.581
The interview deck makes
one honest limit explicit:

2
00:00:03.581 --> 00:00:08.590
published Federal HR 2.0 scope centers
on the federal employee lifecycle,

3
00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:11.875
so a contractor authority
decision is required.

4
00:00:11.875 --> 00:00:17.050
In the processes I have observed,
contractors are tracked in COR spreadsheets.

5
00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.488
This companion goes one step further.

6
00:00:19.488 --> 00:00:24.005
It asks which record should be authoritative
for a contractor, and it adds an

7
00:00:24.005 --> 00:00:28.738
option the main deck doesn't name: the
agency's contractor suitability register.

8
00:00:28.738 --> 00:00:32.513
The one-sentence version: don't
wait for one contractor feed.

9
00:00:32.513 --> 00:00:37.688
Most agencies maintain contractor
information in several operational contexts.

10
00:00:37.688 --> 00:00:42.031
Evaluate them as candidate authorities,
give each fact one authority,

11
00:00:42.031 --> 00:00:45.460
and hang the record on an
accountable federal sponsor.
